From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:28:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/io-pgtable-dart: Add a quirk for S5L8960X table and
 leaf entries
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On the A9 (S8003) PCIe DART the first NVMe submission queue fetch
faulted with

  translation fault: status:0x80000102 stream:0 code:0x2 (NO PMD FOR IOVA)

i.e. "STE invalid" in iOS's naming, at exactly the level where Linux
installs its table entries.

iOS writes these entries differently. AppleS5L8960XDART in the iPad6,11
iOS 16.7.10 kernelcache:
- _createL3Table (0xfffffff005fb33b4) writes each table entry under a
  TTBR as (pa & 0xffffff000) | 3. Linux wrote pa | 1.
- The leaf writer (0xfffffff005fb42e4) writes (pfn << 12) | 2 | valid:
  bit 1 is SP_DIS, as in the DART1 format. Its subpage variant
  (0xfffffff005fb4208) keeps the subpage range at bits 61:50 / 47:36,
  not at the DART1 63:52 / 51:40, and plain leaves leave them clear.

The A10 does the same. The iPadOS 17 T8010 kernelcache's
AppleS5L8960XDART writes table entries as (pa & 0xffffff000) | 3 at
0xfffffff0060f8540 and leaves as pfn << 12 | 2 at 0xfffffff0060f91f0.
So this is a property of every S5L8960X-style DART (A7 to A10), not of
the A9 alone.

Add IO_PGTABLE_QUIRK_APPLE_DART_S5L8960X: table entries get bits 1:0
set, and leaf PTEs leave out the DART1 subpage fields (SP_DIS, bit 1,
is already set on leaves). apple-dart sets it for every S5L8960X DART.

Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
[Orchard: from brkosebay/linux 59e53eb8 (J71t ledger 1.3); applied to
 every S5L8960X DART, T8010 included, with the T8010 kernelcache
 evidence added; the fault-handler table walk is left out (bring-up
 diagnostics, ledger 1.9)]
Co-developed-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c      |  2 ++
 drivers/iommu/io-pgtable-dart.c | 20 +++++++++++++++++---
 include/linux/io-pgtable.h      |  7 +++++++
 3 files changed, 26 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
index f7eee85ea..7e468a73a 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
@@ -834,6 +834,8 @@ static int apple_dart_finalize_domain(struct apple_dart_domain *dart_domain,
 		.coherent_walk = 1,
 		.iommu_dev = dart->dev,
 	};
+	if (dart->hw->type == DART_S5L8960X)
+		pgtbl_cfg.quirks |= IO_PGTABLE_QUIRK_APPLE_DART_S5L8960X;
 
 	dart_domain->pgtbl_ops = alloc_io_pgtable_ops(dart->hw->fmt, &pgtbl_cfg,
 						      &dart_domain->domain);
diff --git a/drivers/iommu/io-pgtable-dart.c b/drivers/iommu/io-pgtable-dart.c
index cbc5d6aa2..f5a375fa3 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/io-pgtable-dart.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/io-pgtable-dart.c
@@ -63,6 +63,12 @@
 /* marks PTE as valid */
 #define APPLE_DART_PTE_VALID		BIT(0)
 
+/*
+ * S5L8960X table entries: iOS AppleS5L8960XDART writes (pa & 0xffffff000) | 3.
+ * With bit 0 alone the DART reports an invalid STE ("NO PMD").
+ */
+#define APPLE_DART_S5L8960X_TABLE_VALID	GENMASK_ULL(1, 0)
+
 /* IOPTE accessors */
 #define iopte_deref(pte, d) __va(iopte_to_paddr(pte, d))
 
@@ -125,9 +131,15 @@ static int dart_init_pte(struct dart_io_pgtable *data,
 			return -EEXIST;
 		}
 
-	/* subpage protection: always allow access to the entire page */
-	pte |= FIELD_PREP(APPLE_DART_PTE_SUBPAGE_START, 0);
-	pte |= FIELD_PREP(APPLE_DART_PTE_SUBPAGE_END, 0xfff);
+	/*
+	 * subpage protection: always allow access to the entire page. S5L8960X
+	 * keeps its subpage range at bits 61:50/47:36 and ignores it with SP_DIS
+	 * (bit 1) set; iOS leaves those bits clear, so do the same.
+	 */
+	if (!(data->iop.cfg.quirks & IO_PGTABLE_QUIRK_APPLE_DART_S5L8960X)) {
+		pte |= FIELD_PREP(APPLE_DART_PTE_SUBPAGE_START, 0);
+		pte |= FIELD_PREP(APPLE_DART_PTE_SUBPAGE_END, 0xfff);
+	}
 
 	pte |= APPLE_DART_PTE_VALID;
 
@@ -145,6 +157,8 @@ static dart_iopte dart_install_table(dart_iopte *table,
 	dart_iopte old, new;
 
 	new = paddr_to_iopte(__pa(table), data) | APPLE_DART_PTE_VALID;
+	if (data->iop.cfg.quirks & IO_PGTABLE_QUIRK_APPLE_DART_S5L8960X)
+		new |= APPLE_DART_S5L8960X_TABLE_VALID;
 
 	/*
 	 * Ensure the table itself is visible before its PTE can be.
diff --git a/include/linux/io-pgtable.h b/include/linux/io-pgtable.h
index e19872e37..93cd501b0 100644
--- a/include/linux/io-pgtable.h
+++ b/include/linux/io-pgtable.h
@@ -93,6 +93,12 @@ struct io_pgtable_cfg {
 	 *	kernel bug, which would justify the WARN_ON().  But for GPU
 	 *	drivers, this could be under control of userspace.  Which
 	 *	deserves an error return, but not to spam dmesg.
+	 *
+	 * IO_PGTABLE_QUIRK_APPLE_DART_S5L8960X: (Apple DART format) A7-A10
+	 *	S5L8960X-style DARTs. Table entries need bits 1:0 set (bit 0
+	 *	alone is an invalid table entry), and leaf PTEs carry no DART1
+	 *	subpage fields (these DARTs keep their subpage range elsewhere
+	 *	and ignore it with bit 1 set).
 	 */
 	#define IO_PGTABLE_QUIRK_ARM_NS			BIT(0)
 	#define IO_PGTABLE_QUIRK_NO_PERMS		BIT(1)
@@ -103,6 +109,7 @@ struct io_pgtable_cfg {
 	#define IO_PGTABLE_QUIRK_ARM_HD			BIT(7)
 	#define IO_PGTABLE_QUIRK_ARM_S2FWB		BIT(8)
 	#define IO_PGTABLE_QUIRK_NO_WARN		BIT(9)
+	#define IO_PGTABLE_QUIRK_APPLE_DART_S5L8960X	BIT(10)
 	unsigned long			quirks;
 	unsigned long			pgsize_bitmap;
 	unsigned int			ias;
